# ==============================================================================
# AquariusOS Plasma Style — the OLD-STYLE copy of metadata.json
# ==============================================================================
# ⚠️ THIS FILE LOOKS REDUNDANT. IT IS NOT. DO NOT DELETE IT.
#
# metadata.json next door is the real description of this theme, and every
# modern part of KDE reads that one. So why is this here?
#
# THE STALE-PICTURE PROBLEM
#   Turning our drawings into actual pixels is slow, so Plasma does it once and
#   keeps the result in a cache file in the user's home folder. If we ship a new
#   version of AquariusOS with redrawn panels, that cache has to be thrown away,
#   or people keep seeing the OLD panels forever.
#
#   Plasma throws it away by putting the theme's version number into the cache
#   file's NAME:  plasma_theme_aquarius_v<version>.kcache
#   New version number, new filename, and Plasma deletes every older one it
#   finds. Simple and reliable.
#
# THE CATCH (checked in KDE's own source: ksvg, imageset_p.cpp)
#   Plasma only bothers looking up the version number if it can first find a
#   file called "config" OR a file called "metadata.desktop" in the theme
#   folder. It does NOT look for metadata.json at that step. No such file, no
#   version in the cache name, and the only thing left to detect a change is
#   the files' timestamps — which this kind of OS deliberately flattens to zero
#   when it builds an image. So timestamps cannot be trusted here.
#
#   Shipping this one small file is what switches the version mechanism on.
#
# WHICH FILE WINS
#   Nothing conflicts. Where both exist, KDE reads metadata.json for the theme's
#   details and plasmarc for its settings; this file is only ever consulted for
#   its existence. The version below is kept in step with metadata.json
#   automatically — both are rewritten during the image build by
#   build_files/plasma-style-version.sh.
#
# Full story: docs/plasma-style.md
# ==============================================================================

[Desktop Entry]
Name=Aquarius
Comment=Smoked-glass panels, dock and popups for AquariusOS

X-KDE-PluginInfo-Name=aquarius
X-KDE-PluginInfo-Author=Stone Harbor Entertainment
X-KDE-PluginInfo-Website=https://github.com/stoneharborent/aquarius-os
X-KDE-PluginInfo-Category=
X-KDE-PluginInfo-License=Apache-2.0
X-KDE-PluginInfo-EnabledByDefault=true

# Rewritten at image-build time. Keep the spelling of this line stable — the
# build script finds it with a plain text match.
X-KDE-PluginInfo-Version=0.0.0-unstamped

X-Plasma-API=5.0
